{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:04b8dcba096fcbbb","name":"Nebula","source":{"id":"source:reference-04b8dcba096fcbbb","title":"Nebula","revision":21393,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:43:03Z","sha256":"d89c9e753fbc96db33bb4c4eea1aa90acfcd2f66355cac86d656e65a65c7935e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21393","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Nebula&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-04b8dcba096fcbbb","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["This stellar gas cloud will someday coalesce and become a star, but for now, it threatens to interfere with your ship's systems."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The brilliant and colorful dust and gases that make up a Nebula might reduce visibility and damage ships' systems, but they are not extremely dangerous. Thus, many creatures seeking to escape from their enemies consider a Nebula an excellent place to hide. If combat breaks out within a Nebula, each side can use the cloud to its advantage, trying to attack the other from a position of concealment.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Nebula Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Keywords:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Atmosphere"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Atmosphere"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Natural"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Natural"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trigger:"]}," A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," begins its turn within a Nebula.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Attack:"]}," +4 vs ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 2d6x2 (-1 step on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},")\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Recurrence:"]}," Hourly, until the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," leaves the Nebula.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":"]}," The following are suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"}," for this Hazard:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," (DC 24):"]}," For 1 hour, the character staves off the effects of Nebula dust and gases. The character can attempt another check each hour for as long as the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," remains within the Nebula."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," The dust and gases from a nebula might affect a Starship's systems. If the Hazard's attack roll exceeds the Starship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"}," by 5 or more, one of its systems (of the Gamemaster's choice) becomes unavailable and cannot be repaired until the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," leaves the Nebula.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
